{"id":"NCT06419374","title":"A Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of Pegozafermin in Participants With Compensated Cirrhosis Due to MASH","official":"A Phase 3 Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of Pegozafermin in Subjects With Compensated Cirrhosis Due to Metabolic Dysfunction-Associated Steatohepatitis (MASH) (ENLIGHTEN-Cirrhosis)","summary":"The study will assess the efficacy and safety of pegozafermin administered in participants with biopsy-confirmed and clinically confirmed compensated cirrhosis due to MASH .","conditions":["Metabolic Dysfunction-Associated Steatohepatitis (MASH) / Nonalcoholic Steatohepatitis (NASH) With Compensated Cirrhosis"],"interventions":[{"type":"BIOLOGICAL","name":"Pegozafermin"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Placebo"}],"criteria":"Key Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Males or non-pregnant females aged between 18 and 75 years (inclusive) at time of signing the informed consent form (ICF).\n* Participants must have type 2 diabetes mellitus diagnosed at least 3 months before screening or at least 2 metabolic risk factors.\n* Evidence of both cirrhosis and MASH etiology, either through a historical biopsy or a biopsy at Screening.\n* Clinical diagnosis of cirrhosis based on the NIT algorithm.\n\nKey Exclusion Criteria:\n\n* Liver disorder other than MASH.\n* History or evidence of hepatic decompensation.\n* History or evidence of hepatocellular carcinoma.\n* Have type 1 diabetes mellitus or poorly controlled type 2 diabetes mellitus.\n* ALT or aspartate aminotransferase (AST) ≥250 units per liter (U/L).\n* Participants taking vitamin E (\\>400 international units \\[IU\\]/day) must be on stable dose for at least 6 months prior to screening.\n\nOther protocol-defined inclusion and exclusion criteria may apply.","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"75 Years","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":1800,"start":"2024-05-24","pcd":"2028-06-30","upd":"2026-10-23","sponsor":"Hoffmann-La Roche","areas":["other"],"central":["Reference Study ID Number: BIO89-100-132 / GC46898 ENLIGHTEN clinical trial / No attachments to email below. · 888-662-6728 (U.S. Only) · global-roche-genentech-trials@gene.com","Fastest response: use the inquiry form. https://www.gene.com/contact-us/submit-medical-inquiry"],"sites":[{"f":"89bio Clinical Study Site","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35205","s":"R","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":"89bio Clinical Study Site"},{"f":"89bio Clinical Study Site","city":"Homewood","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35209","s":"R","lat":33.4718,"lon":-86.8008,"c":"89bio Clinical Study Site"},{"f":"89bio Clinical Study Site","city":"Chandler","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85224","s":"R","lat":33.3062,"lon":-111.8413,"c":"89bio Clinical Study Site"},{"f":"89bio Clinical Study Site","city":"Flagstaff","pr":"Arizona","zip":"86001","s":"STOP","lat":35.1981,"lon":-111.6513,"c":""},{"f":"89bio Clinical Study Site","city":"Peoria","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85381","s":"R","lat":33.5806,"lon":-112.2374,"c":"89bio Clinical Study Site"},{"f":"89bio Clinical Study Site","city":"Phoenix","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85054","s":"R","lat":33.4484,"lon":-112.074,"c":"89bio Clinical Study Site"},{"f":"89bio Clinical Study Site","city":"Sun City","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85351","s":"R","lat":33.5975,"lon":-112.2718,"c":"89bio Clinical Study Site"},{"f":"89bio Clinical Study Site","city":"Tucson","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85712","s":"R","lat":32.2217,"lon":-110.9265,"c":"89bio Clinical Study Site"},{"f":"89bio Clinical Study Site","city":"Tucson","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85715","s":"R","lat":32.2217,"lon":-110.9265,"c":"89bio Clinical Study Site"},{"f":"89bio Clinical Study Site","city":"Tucson","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85716","s":"R","lat":32.2217,"lon":-110.9265,"c":"89bio Clinical Study Site"},{"f":"89bio Clinical Study Site","city":"Little Rock","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72205","s":"R","lat":34.7465,"lon":-92.2896,"c":"89bio Clinical Study Site"},{"f":"89bio Clinical Study Site","city":"North Little Rock